 "finding": "The method's pillars and boxes are its own arithmetic. Averaged over a period of its depth axis, the power it draws at a pixel is that pixel's trajectory energy (correlation 1.000): a pixel whose registration wanders is bright at every depth and, averaged over a thick slab as any rendering does, stands as a column. On the real image such pixels lie where the surface is darker or changes brightness (noise against brightness, correlation -0.24 at Khafre and -0.56 on open plateau), and open plateau with no monument draws the tallest pillars of all; perfectly uniform simulated ground draws none. Along a column the power rises and falls every 13 m of the relabelled axis, its resolution: the bands. At the surface and again at each repeat depth, 648 m and 1296 m relabelled, every steering phase is the same, so the power there is each pixel's average offset (ratio 0.994, correlation 0.996): the blocks. Below 648 m the picture repeats (correlation 0.968)."
